 1071 "Simplify the expression $5k - 3k + 2k - t$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054375 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2da17fa4-3fb1-50b9-a317-47c38107ff60" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054375 #edb/ref 1074 "We have three like terms, $5k, -3k$, and $2k$.\n\nTo collect these like terms, we combine them into a single term, adding their coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n5k - 3k + 2k - t &=  \\\\\n(5 - 3 + 2)k - t &=  \\\\\n&= 4k - t\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054376 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12797" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054376 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify the expression $6a+1-2a$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054376 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d902668d-ffe0-53bb-a360-2e4e472404f0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054376 #edb/ref 1074 "We rearrange the terms so that the like terms, $6a$ and $-2a$, are together.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 6a+1-2a \\\\[5pt] &= \\underbrace{6a-2a}_{a \\textrm{terms}}+ 1 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we combine the like terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\underbrace{6a-2a}+ 1 \\\\[5pt] &= (6-2)a + 1 \\\\[5pt] &= 4a + 1& \\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054377 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12798" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054377 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify the expression $2.5x+2y-x+1.5y$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054377 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c6e112dd-4c10-5ce6-87a9-6066a366dd33" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054377 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we group the like terms.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 2.5x+2y-x+1.5y \\\\[5pt] &= \\underbrace{2.5x-x}_{x \\textrm{terms}}+\\underbrace{2y+1.5y}_{y \\textrm{terms}} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we combine the like terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\underbrace{2.5x-x}+\\underbrace{2y+1.5y} \\\\[5pt] &= (2.5-1)x + (2+1.5)y \\\\[5pt] &= 1.5x + 3.5y \\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054788 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048546 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054788 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048549 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054788 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048911 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054788 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049264 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054788 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055026 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054788 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055218 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054788 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055394 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054788 #edb/ref 1039 "Simplifying Expressions With Two or Three Terms" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054788 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186054374 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054788 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "6e3d5ce2-c3a5-5787-88f6-a76b223ece1e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054789 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055386 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054789 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055393 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054789 #edb/ref 1039 "Simplifying Expressions With Four Terms" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054789 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186054375 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054789 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "eb8ce725-4a41-544c-b705-743a7ef9635d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054790 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055207 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054790 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055381 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054790 #edb/ref 1039 "Rearranging an Expression Before Collecting Like Terms" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054790 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186054376 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054790 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "342e8283-f3a1-5923-8788-1a489ae058c5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054791 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048207 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054791 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055245 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054791 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186055389 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054791 #edb/ref 1039 "Collecting Groups of Like Terms" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054791 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186054377 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054791 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "d7162d23-7674-5319-9f00-ca1a37ecccd3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054884 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186055808 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054884 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186055809 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054884 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186055810 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054884 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186055811 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054884 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186055812 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054884 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054884 #edb/ref 1045 "Collecting Like Terms in Linear Expressions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054884 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186055808 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054884 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050452 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054884 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "72b6726f-b68f-5ab6-9c1f-8455335fd490" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055381 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186053523 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055381 #edb/ref 1069 "q-563" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055381 #edb/ref 1071 "What is $13x - 2y + 5x + 1$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055381 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a35d688d-c263-50c4-b62e-c79c29a24f63" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055808 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055809 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055808 #edb/ref 1061 53080 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055808 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "be184f2e-07fc-5e2d-8b00-c1117788f171" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055808 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186056007 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055809 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055810 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055809 #edb/ref 1061 53081 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055809 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "08409be9-255d-5bc1-a5b8-6d0b41d026e7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055809 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186054788 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055810 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055811 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055810 #edb/ref 1061 53085 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055810 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e4469d1c-c914-5c3f-ba7b-86b664dd3254" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055810 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186054789 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055811 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055812 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055811 #edb/ref 1061 53088 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055811 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5885aa4d-be69-5e80-973b-720b6c256aa9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055811 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186054790 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055812 #edb/ref 1061 53091 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055812 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c456479e-8d24-5aa9-b6e2-c78f4c25360d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055812 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186054791 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056007 #edb/ref 1064 "Remember that two terms are called **like terms** if they have the same variable part.\n\nAn expression with different terms can often be simplified by **collecting like terms**.\n\nFor example, consider the following expression:\n$2x+3x$\n\nThe terms $2x$ and $3x$ are like terms because they both have a variable part of $x$.\n\nWhenever we have two or more like terms in an expression, we can combine them into a single term. Here, we can combine the like terms $2x$ and $3x$ into a single term by adding their coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x + 3x &=  \\\\\n(2 + 3)x &=  \\\\\n&= 5x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056007 #edb/ref 1065 8021 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056007 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "bf438600-1106-5d9f-b7c3-6c7c18d3bb77" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056007 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
